Items dropped close together are hard to pick: the labels pile up on top of each other, a click often hits the wrong item, and 10 sticks take 10 clicks. With this mod each pile has one label, and the number on it is what you get with one click.

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Merged labels.[/b] Items of the same kind within 2 m merge into one label with the total, such as "Stick (11)".[/*]
[*][b]One click for the whole pile.[/b] Click a label to pick all the items on it, with one pickup animation. With the labels off, click an item to also pick the same items within 2 m.[/*]
[*][b]Collect clay and mud in one click.[/b] Collect from clay, mud, or sand with your hands, and one action takes the same kind of ground within 2 m: up to 69 normal tries, each with its normal yield and cost. One message shows the total. Dirt, tilled ground, Clay Deposits, and digging with a shovel stay as in the game.[/*]
[*][b]No overlapping labels.[/b] Labels move up or down until each has its own space, also the labels of stockpiles, resources, and constructions.[/*]
[*][b]Action hints above the hotbar.[/b] Hints such as "LMB Pick up" or "Ctrl + LMB Take apart" move from the label to a panel at the bottom center of the screen, in the game's style. They no longer cover other labels or the item you hover.[/*]
[*][b]The game's rules apply.[/b] Inventory limits stay the same, and items that do not fit stay on the ground. The whole pile takes the time of one pickup. Items that go into your hands or onto your back are picked one at a time.[/*]
[*][b]Save safety.[/b] The mod writes nothing to your save, so you can remove it at any time. Made for single player: co-op is not tested.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]The Last Plague: Blight 0.12.7 or later.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelastplagueblight/mods/9]BepInEx for The Last Plague: Blight[/url].[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/thelastplagueblight/mods/9]BepInEx[/url].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\The Last Plague\BepInEx\plugins\ProximityPickup.dll[/code][/*][/list]

[size=4][b]Uninstall[/b][/size]
Delete [font=Courier New]ProximityPickup.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder.

[size=4][b]Configuration[/b][/size]
To change mod settings, edit [font=Courier New]BepInEx\config\com.ivmakk.thelastplagueblight.proximitypickup.cfg[/font] while the game is closed (see [url=https://github.com/ivmakk-tlpb/tlpb-proximity-pickup/blob/main/CONFIG.md]CONFIG.md[/url] for every setting). Changes apply at the next game start.

